DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The wwccssdduupp() function is the wide‐character equivalent of the ssttrrdduupp(3)
       function.   It  allocates and returns a new wide‐character string whose
       initial contents is a duplicate of the wide‐character string pointed to
       by _s.

       Memory for the new wide‐character string is  obtained  with  mmaalllloocc(3),
       and should be freed with ffrreeee(3).

